same dimensions.\n\nFirst, notice that $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $Y$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $u$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nNow, let's consider each expression in turn:\n\n- The dimensions of $YX$ are $2\\times 2,$ and the dimensions of $Y\\,\\text{diag}(u)$ are $2\\times 3.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression I is *not* well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $X$ are $3\\times 2,$ and the dimensions of $Yu$ are $2\\times 1.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression II is *not* well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $Y\\,\\text{diag}(u)$ are $2\\times 3,$ and the dimensions of $YX{X}^{T}$ are $2\\times 3.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression III is well-defined.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f680b101-94a2-558f-9708-756d2ba22da2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f680b101-94a2-558f-9708-756d2ba22da2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f680b101-94a2-558f-9708-756d2ba22da2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-368e5c38-687c-5476-a766-53fe59679efb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a81f915c-2e4f-5036-ade2-5fb2255941e1" "answer-a859c734-1278-56c3-b313-37ad8c178a6c" "answer-a2de33de-7c02-5cb9-b000-8fd4ffa0668b" "answer-cee12af1-4ad7-5e93-a79a-1c4026db489e" "answer-368e5c38-687c-5476-a766-53fe59679efb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a81f915c-2e4f-5036-ade2-5fb2255941e1" :answer/id #uuid "a81f915c-2e4f-5036-ade2-5fb2255941e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a859c734-1278-56c3-b313-37ad8c178a6c" :answer/id #uuid "a859c734-1278-56c3-b313-37ad8c178a6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2de33de-7c02-5cb9-b000-8fd4ffa0668b" :answer/id #uuid "a2de33de-7c02-5cb9-b000-8fd4ffa0668b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cee12af1-4ad7-5e93-a79a-1c4026db489e" :answer/id #uuid "cee12af1-4ad7-5e93-a79a-1c4026db489e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-368e5c38-687c-5476-a766-53fe59679efb" :answer/id #uuid "368e5c38-687c-5476-a766-53fe59679efb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208845 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0f56bf75-c034-5aab-87bb-3f506f067872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f56bf75-c034-5aab-87bb-3f506f067872" :question/id #uuid "0f56bf75-c034-5aab-87bb-3f506f067872" :question/math-academy-id "q-350412" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices above, write the following expression as a Hadamard product. Here $(\\,\\cdot \\,)$ denotes matrix multiplication.\n\n| $(AB)\\cdot (By)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $⊙$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-6$ |  |  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "The Hadamard product of two compatible vectors $u$ and $v$ can be expressed as the matrix product\n\n$$\nv⊙u=\\text{diag}(v)u.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nBy=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB)\\cdot (By) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\text{diag}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}])[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]⊙[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68f52881-eb76-51b7-8183-8acacfe3a8e3" "answer-field-cde49d9c-ec17-5210-bdd7-9e30e90fa8b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68f52881-eb76-51b7-8183-8acacfe3a8e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "68f52881-eb76-51b7-8183-8acacfe3a8e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d8df6e2-fe2b-50c4-8d6d-bfcfdcb03b07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d8df6e2-fe2b-50c4-8d6d-bfcfdcb03b07"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d8df6e2-fe2b-50c4-8d6d-bfcfdcb03b07" :answer/id #uuid "2d8df6e2-fe2b-50c4-8d6d-bfcfdcb03b07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cde49d9c-ec17-5210-bdd7-9e30e90fa8b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde49d9c-ec17-5210-bdd7-9e30e90fa8b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c6019430-865a-5e00-8e5e-9f4fec670079" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6019430-865a-5e00-8e5e-9f4fec670079"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6019430-865a-5e00-8e5e-9f4fec670079" :answer/id #uuid "c6019430-865a-5e00-8e5e-9f4fec670079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208844 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-949652ef-4c40-590b-96ed-3051cee3c306" "question-68db0f47-da70-5824-b3d3-6f9cad326490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-949652ef-4c40-590b-96ed-3051cee3c306" :question/id #uuid "949652ef-4c40-590b-96ed-3051cee3c306" :question/math-academy-id "q-350493" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nA⊙B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,A⊙C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nfind $A⊙(B+C).$" :question/worked-solution "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the distributivity over the addition of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A⊙(B+C) & =A⊙B+A⊙C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+5 & 4+(-3) \\\\ 3+2 & -2+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f521befc-49de-525d-bb6c-09034e61c454"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f521befc-49de-525d-bb6c-09034e61c454" :answer-field/id #uuid "f521befc-49de-525d-bb6c-09034e61c454" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2828159a-8410-56f3-9efb-1ceb5129dd0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e6c4830-f8dc-59ec-afda-b68feab4a6a7" "answer-99e69295-3d01-5049-930d-3445788a8790" "answer-f0e8fae5-91ca-5766-8b3c-4c78391343e3" "answer-2828159a-8410-56f3-9efb-1ceb5129dd0f" "answer-8439cea5-6452-5e18-b89d-aa00cedaf1de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e6c4830-f8dc-59ec-afda-b68feab4a6a7" :answer/id #uuid "5e6c4830-f8dc-59ec-afda-b68feab4a6a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99e69295-3d01-5049-930d-3445788a8790" :answer/id #uuid "99e69295-3d01-5049-930d-3445788a8790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0e8fae5-91ca-5766-8b3c-4c78391343e3" :answer/id #uuid "f0e8fae5-91ca-5766-8b3c-4c78391343e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2828159a-8410-56f3-9efb-1ceb5129dd0f" :answer/id #uuid "2828159a-8410-56f3-9efb-1ceb5129dd0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8439cea5-6452-5e18-b89d-aa00cedaf1de" :answer/id #uuid "8439cea5-6452-5e18-b89d-aa00cedaf1de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-68db0f47-da70-5824-b3d3-6f9cad326490" :question/id #uuid "68db0f47-da70-5824-b3d3-6f9cad326490" :question/math-academy-id "q-350504" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\nA⊙B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,A⊙C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfind $A⊙(B+C)+A⊙(B⊙C).$" :question/worked-solution "For compatible matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ and scalar $\\alpha ,$ the Hadamard product has the following properties:\n\n- Commutativity:\n\n$$\nA⊙B=B⊙A\n$$\n\n- Associativity:\n\n$$\n(A⊙B)⊙C=A⊙(B⊙C)\n$$\n\n- Distributivity over Addition:\n\n$$\nA⊙(B+C)=A⊙B+A⊙C\n$$\n\n- Scalar Distributivity:\n\n$$\n\\alpha (A⊙B)=(\\alpha A)⊙B=A⊙(\\alpha B)\n$$\n\nIn this case, by the associativity and distributivity over addition of the Hadamard product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A⊙(B+C)+A⊙(B⊙C) & =A⊙B+A⊙C+(A⊙B)⊙C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]⊙[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4 & 2+6 \\\\ 1+6 & 3+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c05be3c-7d25-5dfd-8e69-447a6a2a04e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c05be3c-7d25-5dfd-8e69-447a6a2a04e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c05be3c-7d25-5dfd-8e69-447a6a2a04e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1440de-fe62-5405-8d7c-43173b4ade2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dc3f7e36-8366-578d-8708-012e7950357b" "answer-121e66b4-70e7-5b38-a11e-65d067c24a87" "answer-17423c56-ad3b-5cbd-b3f2-198c80452668" "answer-f04c7d01-21d9-5652-9799-840c490732ad" "answer-cb1440de-fe62-5405-8d7c-43173b4ade2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc3f7e36-8366-578d-8708-012e7950357b" :answer/id #uuid "dc3f7e36-8366-578d-8708-012e7950357b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-121e66b4-70e7-5b38-a11e-65d067c24a87" :answer/id #uuid "121e66b4-70e7-5b38-a11e-65d067c24a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17423c56-ad3b-5cbd-b3f2-198c80452668" :answer/id #uuid "17423c56-ad3b-5cbd-b3f2-198c80452668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f04c7d01-21d9-5652-9799-840c490732ad" :answer/id #uuid "f04c7d01-21d9-5652-9799-840c490732ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb1440de-fe62-5405-8d7c-43173b4ade2f" :answer/id #uuid "cb1440de-fe62-5405-8d7c-43173b4ade2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b99ebc85-8cef-5385-a2b1-1c327e93470d" :activity/id 